 "decision": "p_corr < 0.05: anomaly with causes not separable by this test: chance (1 anomalous curve out of the family), residual foregrounds/point sources inside the common mask, mask-edge effects, and component-separation residuals (diagnostic: gate calibration-check var_ratio_sim_over_data=0.9814, i.e. sims carry ~1.9% less unmasked-pixel variance than the data, a plausible partial cause -- power beyond lmax=384 and/or the ud_grade 2048->128 downsampling of a 5-arcmin map are candidates not excluded by this test; neither a failure of M0 nor support for an alternative. At the sensitivity from the string power table: this test detects (p_corr<0.05) a great-circle-step injection at A/sigma=0.2 (~4.8% added pixel variance) in 52% of sims, and at A/sigma=0.4 in 100% of sims (of 200 sims per amplitude). No K3xT2 statement."
